---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service | LDiHK">
  <LegalPage heading="Terms of Service" updated="19 October 2026">
    <h2>1. Provider and scope</h2>
    <p>
      These terms govern the use of the LDiHK website and analytics console (the "Service"), provided by
      LDiHK, Munich, Germany
      ("we"). Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ldihk.xyz">contact@ldihk.xyz</a>.
      By uploading data or using the console you accept these terms. How we handle personal data is described in our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. The Service</h2>
    <p>
      LDiHK lets you upload data exports from social media platforms, analyses your usage patterns and compares them with
      other people and with published research. The Service is a free prototype created for the EuroTech x Hong Kong Talent Exchange Hackathon 2026 in Munich; it is not a commercial or insurance product. Features may change, be
      interrupted or be discontinued at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      All results, including the risk indicator on the health tab, are for information and self-reflection only. They are
      based on statistical associations from research and on estimates (for example of watch time), are not a diagnosis
      and do not replace advice from a doctor or psychotherapist. If you are in distress, contact a health professional or
      your local emergency number.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who may use the Service</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 16 years old, or have the consent of a parent or legal guardian.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Your LDiHK-ID</h2>
    <p>
      Your LDiHK-ID is the only key to your data. Keep it secret and do not share it. We cannot restore a lost ID, and
      anyone who knows your ID can view and delete your data. Tell us immediately if you believe someone else has it.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your uploads</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Upload only data exports of your own accounts, which you are entitled to use.</li>
      <li>Do not upload other people's data, illegal content or files designed to harm the Service.</li>
      <li>
        You keep all rights to your data. You allow us to process it only as far as needed to provide the Service as
        described in the Privacy Policy. You can delete it at any time with "Delete My Data".
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not try to access other users' data, bypass rate limits or security measures, overload the Service, or use it
      for automated mass requests. We may block access that violates these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      The Service uses YouTube API Services. By using the Service you also agree to the
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener" target="_blank">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
      LDiHK is not affiliated with or endorsed by YouTube, Google, Instagram, Meta or TikTok.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Availability and warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided free of charge and "as is". We do not guarantee that it is always available, error-free or
      that results are complete or accurate. Statutory rights that cannot be excluded remain unaffected.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      We are liable without limitation for intent and gross negligence, for injury to life, body or health, and under
      mandatory statutory provisions (such as product liability law). For slight negligence we are liable only for the
      breach of essential obligations, limited to the typical, foreseeable damage. Otherwise our liability is excluded,
      to the extent permitted by law.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Ending use</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using the Service at any time and delete your data with "Delete My Data". We may discontinue the Service;
      if we do, we will delete all user data.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The current version is always available here; for significant changes we will inform
      you in the console. If you continue to use the Service after a change, the new terms apply.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      The law of Germany applies, excluding the UN
      Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. If you are a consumer, this does not deprive you of the
      protection of mandatory provisions of the law of your country of residence.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
